    "description": "This course aims to provide a broad introduction to contemporary topics in materials science, with an emphasis on relating materials chemistry to their unique properties and real-world applications. We will discuss fundamental chemistry governing the properties of various materials, and gain insights on current material-based technologies and research. Upon completing this course, you will be able to appreciate the importance of materials in our everyday lives and explain their working principles. This course will provide students an opportunity to gain expertise in both chemistry and materials sciences, thereby supporting you for future career in relevant industries (e.g. semiconductors, energy and biomedical) and/or materials research.",
