    "code": "CS2024",
    "name": "WEB DESIGN & TECHNOLOGIES",
    "description": "The course covers a brief history of hypertext and the World Wide Web, and gives a broad overview of technologies used in Web design. Students will be taught how to design, implement and maintain Web-based sites using authoring and scripting languages, content creation, management and digital media tools. Students will learn how to implement the latest strategies to develop third generation Websites, evaluate design tools, discuss future technology standards and explore the incompatibility issues surrounding current browsers.",
