    "description": "This course introduces the concepts and design of distributed systems. 1.\tFoundations: characteristics of distributed systems, architectural models, fundamental models, interprocess communication. 2.\tMiddleware: remote method invocation, remote procedure call, name services, CORBA. 3.\tSystem Infrastructure: distributed file systems, peer-to-peer systems. 4.\tDistributed Algorithms: clock synchronization, logical and vector clocks, distributed mutual exclusion, election algorithms, consensus algorithms, replication and fault tolerance.",
