    "code": "EE3015",
    "name": "POWER SYSTEMS & CONVERSION",
    "description": "The aim of this course is to provide fundamental knowledge for B.Eng. (EEE) students who wish to specialize in power engineering in their profession. It introduces you to the overall structure of the electric power supply system, starting from power generation to power transmission, distribution and power conversion. It includes basic concepts of power systems operation and techniques of solid-state power conversions, electric drives and applications of power electronics.. Contents: Fundamentals of Power Systems. System Operation. Power Conversion. Electromechanical Power Conversion Systems. Applications of Power Electronics in power systems.",
