    "description": "The course wi ll discuss sustainability from perspectives of various disciplines, including humanities, business, policy, economics, and science. Students will learn about sustainability through a case study of oil palm plantation. The course will be composed of the following 6 modules. The course is supplemented by Module SI , which helps broadening students\\' perspectives on sustainability. Module I : General Introduction Module 2: The Global Seeding of Oil Palm Module 3: Recent Expansion of Oil Palm in South East Asia: How and Why did this happen? Module 4: How is Oil Palm Production Affecting Environment, Climate and Human Society? Module 5: Making Oil Palm More Sustainable Module 6: General Conclusions Module SI: National Geographic (Nat. Geo) talk",
