    "code": "HC4063",
    "name": "A STUDY OF SINOPHONE CULTURE IN SINGAPORE & MALAYSIA",
    "description": "1.\tExplaining the concept of Sinophone as well as examining the ideology of \\'Imperialism,\\' \\'Colonialism,\\' \\'Nationalism,\\' \\'Cultural China,\\' and \\'Chinese diaspora\\'. 2.\tLooking deeply at the five dimensions of Sinophone culture - language identity, cultural identity, class identity, national identity and gender identity. 3.\tBringing together local Singaporean and Malaysian Sinophone audiovisual texts, such as Chinese/dialect films, songs, and literature as well as using historical materials such as old Chinese newspapers and periodicals in Singapore and Malaya as a reference to rethink the Singaporean and Malaysian Chinese identity",
