    "code": "HL4023",
    "name": "ADVANCED STUDIES IN AMERICAN LITERATURE",
    "description": "This course deepens understanding of American literature by engaging with challenging works of fiction and poetry that experiment with form and also engage with the nation\\'s history, in order to produce a critical perspective of the twentieth century, especially in terms of how industrialization and modernization have led a to crisis in subjectivity that demands a revised understanding of ontology and moral foundations.",
