    "code": "HL4034",
    "name": "BRITISH ASIAN LITERATURE",
    "description": "In the first three novels (by Syal, Ali and Mo respectively), we will look at how writers depict double-consciousness, how they negotiate subject positions within and between different socio-cultural traditions/formations. With the last two novels (by Gunesekera and Gupta respectively), we will engage definitional concerns, that is, we will look at how writers try to escape the perennial absorptionism versus enclavism debate that constrains \\'minority writing.\\'",
    "prereq": "HL1001",
