    "code": "HP4109",
    "name": "CLINICAL INTERVIEWING & COUNSELLING SKILLS",
    "description": "This course aims to introduce opportunities for students to have hands-on experience in developing and refining a range of emphatic listening, micro-counselling, and clinical interviewing skills. These are skills that are important in the developmental and maintenance of a productive therapeutic alliance, and for effective counselling and psychotherapy in applied clinical settings.",
