    "code": "HY0001",
    "name": "ETHICS & MORAL REASONING",
    "description": "HY0001 will introduce students to three major ethical theories\\' utilitarianism, Kant\\'s deontology, and virtue ethics. Then, four weeks will be devoted to teaching the ethical principles underlying academic integrity, research ethics, and intellectual property. Finally, students will discuss issues related to the ethics of environmental sustainability and conservation. All the while, students will be challenged apply the ethical theories learned to concrete moral problems, including world poverty, corporate accountability and whistleblowing, and workplace discrimination.",
