    "description": "This interdisciplinary course aims to arm you with the knowledge required to appreciate rapidly growing cross-disciplinary research frontiers that interface physics, information science and computation. You will be introduced to the fundamentals of classical and quantum information science and their underlying physical principles, which will give you the necessary expertise to follow and initiate research in the blossoming fields of information physics, quantum information, and quantum computation.",
